    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zōdĭăcus</span></b> ,
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωδιακός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the zodiac</i> (pure Lat. orbis signifer), <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Arat. 317</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 13, 9, 6</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zōdĭăcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of the zodiac</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zodiacum diastema,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zodiacus tractus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zodiaca hospitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1</span></i>
			, § 5. 
			</div>
